1
00:00:08,480 --> 00:00:13,490
RACING GIRLS COLLAB CAFÉ!
IN PREPARATION

2
00:00:17,490 --> 00:00:19,770
It feels so realistic.

3
00:00:19,770 --> 00:00:20,750
It does!

4
00:00:20,750 --> 00:00:26,420
I didn't know what to expect when you said 
you wanted to include one of the vehicles,

5
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:30,720
but it turned out great. It really brings 
the world of <i>Racing Girls</i> to life.

6
00:00:31,390 --> 00:00:32,960
Thank you very much!

7
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:37,460
What about the merch for that shelf?

8
00:00:38,090 --> 00:00:40,580
It's supposed to be delivered 
first thing in the morning.

9
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:43,800
Is that so?

10
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:45,140
Senpai?

11
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:47,460
It's nothing.

12
00:00:47,460 --> 00:00:48,230
What else...

13
00:00:53,210 --> 00:00:56,240
The outfits for the staff 
turned out great, as well!

14
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:00,620
<i>They're so cute.</i>

15
00:01:01,830 --> 00:01:06,030
<i>Does Kamegawa like these kinds of clothes?</i>

16
00:01:08,580 --> 00:01:10,130
Looks great!

17
00:01:10,130 --> 00:01:12,660
I'm looking forward to tomorrow.

18
00:01:14,170 --> 00:01:15,120
Yes, ma'am!

19
00:01:17,430 --> 00:01:21,100
MY AWKWARD SENPAI

20
00:02:46,020 --> 00:02:51,020
EPISODE 8: I'M GONNA BE A MAID!

21
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:49,770
"I'm Gonna Be a Maid!"

22
00:02:59,190 --> 00:03:00,710
Oh! Senpai!

23
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:02,780
Oh. Hey.

24
00:03:02,780 --> 00:03:04,270
Good morning.

25
00:03:05,010 --> 00:03:06,590
Are you going somewhere?

26
00:03:06,590 --> 00:03:09,120
Yeah. I'm headed to Kamegawa's job site.

27
00:03:09,790 --> 00:03:12,350
Oh, yeah! Today's the first day for that café!

28
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:16,130
You look excited for it.

29
00:03:16,130 --> 00:03:17,360
Do I?

30
00:03:18,570 --> 00:03:19,630
Not really.

31
00:03:19,630 --> 00:03:21,790
Can I come with you?

32
00:03:21,790 --> 00:03:23,240
I don't mind, but...

33
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:25,600
What about your duties?

34
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:27,100
No worries!

35
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:29,350
I'll use this as material
for the company newsletter!

36
00:03:33,910 --> 00:03:35,330
I see.

37
00:03:35,330 --> 00:03:37,610
So it's a collaboration with an app game.

38
00:03:37,610 --> 00:03:38,580
Yup.

39
00:03:38,580 --> 00:03:42,110
I put Kamegawa in charge from 
the project's proposal stage.

40
00:03:42,110 --> 00:03:45,010
It's his first project, 
so I'm sure it was challenging,

41
00:03:45,010 --> 00:03:46,160
but he did his best—

42
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:48,170
You really are excited for this.

43
00:03:48,170 --> 00:03:48,950
Wha—

44
00:03:48,950 --> 00:03:51,210
You don't have to stare at me like that!

45
00:03:51,650 --> 00:03:53,510
Here's how it is.

46
00:03:53,510 --> 00:03:58,670
Today's the day we see the results of 
the job Kamegawa has been in charge of.

47
00:03:59,420 --> 00:04:01,560
Kamegawa sure is lucky.

48
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:02,140
Huh?

49
00:04:02,140 --> 00:04:06,250
A mentor who puts in this much effort 
is hard to come by, you know?

50
00:04:06,250 --> 00:04:09,930
Lately, that guy's been
 oozing this happy aura.

51
00:04:10,260 --> 00:04:12,490
Happy aura?

52
00:04:13,930 --> 00:04:16,940
Look at that! Business is booming!

53
00:04:16,940 --> 00:04:18,330
Looks like it.

54
00:04:18,330 --> 00:04:20,940
We can't let our guard down yet, 
but it's off to a good start.

55
00:04:21,280 --> 00:04:24,450
But there's still time before 
the store even opens.

56
00:04:24,450 --> 00:04:26,110
Isn't everyone here kinda early?

57
00:04:26,110 --> 00:04:28,350
That goes for you, too, Senpai.

58
00:04:28,350 --> 00:04:31,410
The one thing you need for 
any opening day is motivation.

59
00:04:33,390 --> 00:04:34,560
<i>That's right!</i>

60
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:38,700
<i>New software requires automatic 
downloads upon pre-order.</i>

61
00:04:38,700 --> 00:04:42,420
<i>And new apps gift items when you pre-register.</i>

62
00:04:42,420 --> 00:04:46,930
<i>I'm not exaggeratin' when I say the battle's 
already started before it's even begun!</i>

63
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:48,910
S-Senpai?

64
00:04:48,910 --> 00:04:53,860
Besides, I need to be prepared as 
a senpai. In case something happens.

65
00:04:57,370 --> 00:04:58,150
Well...

66
00:04:58,150 --> 00:05:02,170
he'll probably be all right, since he's 
got a good head on his shoulders.

67
00:05:03,610 --> 00:05:05,600
Do you really think so?

68
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:07,960
Kamegawa can be a bit airheaded at times—

69
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:09,260
I'm terribly sorry!

70
00:05:09,660 --> 00:05:11,860
I'll make preparations for this immediately.

71
00:05:11,860 --> 00:05:16,060
Please tell me the areas that won't 
interfere with your opening tasks.

72
00:05:16,490 --> 00:05:18,670
I'll finish preparing the display right now.

73
00:05:22,750 --> 00:05:25,030
Thank you for helping me.

74
00:05:25,630 --> 00:05:27,490
How did this happen?

75
00:05:27,490 --> 00:05:31,640
The packages arrived just a moment ago.

76
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:33,780
Weren't they supposed to be here 
first thing in the morning?

77
00:05:34,140 --> 00:05:37,140
Apparently, there was a mistake 
on the supplier's end.

78
00:05:37,140 --> 00:05:40,600
What? But that's not even your fault.

79
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:43,930
No. It is your fault for 
scheduling things so tightly.

80
00:05:45,950 --> 00:05:48,000
Yes. I'm sorry.

81
00:05:49,570 --> 00:05:50,410
And...

82
00:05:50,950 --> 00:05:53,380
it's also my fault for neglecting to check.

83
00:05:53,380 --> 00:05:54,410
I apologize.

84
00:05:54,410 --> 00:05:54,920
What?

85
00:05:54,920 --> 00:05:57,880
N-Not at all! Why are you 
the one apologizing, Senpai?

86
00:05:57,880 --> 00:05:59,380
He's right, Senpai.

87
00:05:59,690 --> 00:06:00,690
Hold on.

88
00:06:00,690 --> 00:06:02,630
Why are you even here, Hotta?

89
00:06:02,630 --> 00:06:03,720
Anyway—

90
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:06,030
We can discuss this further 
once we finish the displays.

91
00:06:06,030 --> 00:06:07,810
There's still time before the store opens.

92
00:06:07,810 --> 00:06:08,660
Yes, ma'am!

93
00:06:09,690 --> 00:06:12,970
<i>I-I've done it now!</i>

94
00:06:12,970 --> 00:06:15,950
<i>When I heard him say the delivery 
was due first thing in the mornin',</i>

95
00:06:15,950 --> 00:06:19,650
<i>I kept my mouth shut 'cuz I figured 
I shouldn't nag him too much...</i>

96
00:06:19,650 --> 00:06:22,130
<i>I need to actually say what I need to say.</i>

97
00:06:22,130 --> 00:06:23,900
Excuse me, Kamegawa-san?

98
00:06:23,900 --> 00:06:24,650
Yes!

99
00:06:24,650 --> 00:06:26,220
What's the matter?

100
00:06:26,220 --> 00:06:29,410
Three of our part-timers just called out.

101
00:06:29,410 --> 00:06:30,480
What?!

102
00:06:30,910 --> 00:06:35,450
I can contact other employees, 
but I doubt they can arrive immediately.

103
00:06:35,910 --> 00:06:38,020
I-I see...

104
00:06:38,020 --> 00:06:42,590
I can reach out to a few event 
companies I've worked with before.

105
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:45,800
I'm so sorry to cause you trouble.

106
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:47,160
Don't worry about it.

107
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:49,800
No one could have predicted this.

108
00:06:50,750 --> 00:06:52,480
Thank you so much.

109
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:53,230
Yeah.

110
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:58,310
<i>Looks like we can handle 
the displays somehow,</i>

111
00:06:58,920 --> 00:07:01,630
<i>but to overcome the lack of 
hands on the main floor...</i>

112
00:07:10,830 --> 00:07:11,820
Hotta.

113
00:07:11,820 --> 00:07:13,360
Where's Kannawa-senpai?

114
00:07:13,740 --> 00:07:16,570
It sounds like help will 
arrive in the afternoon.

115
00:07:16,570 --> 00:07:18,340
Oh, that's good.

116
00:07:18,340 --> 00:07:20,420
Let's tell Senpai quickly and...

117
00:07:20,420 --> 00:07:21,280
Huh?

118
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:22,960
She's not here.

119
00:07:23,340 --> 00:07:24,520
Now that I think about it,

120
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:27,710
she took off over there after 
making a serious face.

121
00:07:28,990 --> 00:07:31,220
I knew it! She's furious!

122
00:07:31,220 --> 00:07:33,230
If only I'd done a better job!

123
00:07:33,230 --> 00:07:35,340
Stop moping already.

124
00:07:35,340 --> 00:07:37,220
Regret won't make up for your mistakes.

125
00:07:37,220 --> 00:07:40,150
I know, but still...

126
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:41,980
Wait, what?

127
00:07:41,980 --> 00:07:43,270
Senpai?

128
00:07:43,270 --> 00:07:47,480
If you have the time to stand around 
like that, then plan your next steps.

129
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:49,710
My next... That's right!

130
00:07:49,710 --> 00:07:51,800
About the additional staff members...

131
00:07:53,550 --> 00:07:54,870
As for me...

132
00:07:55,870 --> 00:07:57,950
If I want redemption...

133
00:07:59,030 --> 00:08:00,370
I'll do anything to achieve it.

134
00:08:02,310 --> 00:08:03,270
What?!

135
00:08:06,270 --> 00:08:08,420
Why are you wearing a maid outfit, Senpai?!

136
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:11,460
If they're short-staffed, 
we should help them.

137
00:08:11,460 --> 00:08:14,460
If I'm to work here, 
of course I need to dress like this.

138
00:08:14,460 --> 00:08:17,820
Master's dreams would be 
crushed if you didn't, after all.

139
00:08:17,820 --> 00:08:20,180
I-I see...

140
00:08:20,180 --> 00:08:22,490
So stop your brooding.

141
00:08:22,490 --> 00:08:25,060
If you have the time to do that, get to work!

142
00:08:25,060 --> 00:08:27,190
Yes, ma'am! You're absolutely right!

143
00:08:28,690 --> 00:08:30,470
<i>That wasn't it!</i>

144
00:08:30,730 --> 00:08:34,570
<i>C'mon! There must've been 
a nicer way to do that!</i>

145
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:35,820
Hey!

146
00:08:35,820 --> 00:08:36,700
Yes?

147
00:08:43,710 --> 00:08:45,820
<i>All right! I did it!</i>

148
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:52,260
Senpai! That's not how 
you encourage someone!

149
00:08:56,330 --> 00:08:58,430
Welcome home.

150
00:08:58,820 --> 00:09:02,180
Welcome home, Master.

151
00:09:02,810 --> 00:09:05,690
FUEL

152
00:09:03,350 --> 00:09:05,690
Th-Thank you for waiting.

153
00:09:13,150 --> 00:09:16,660
MOE MOE ENERGY CHARGE
SPECIAL RACING RICE

154
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:16,000
Isn't this supposed to...

155
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:20,010
F-For victory!

156
00:09:20,010 --> 00:09:22,580
Energy charge of love!

157
00:09:23,180 --> 00:09:27,000
Moe! Moe! Fill 'er up with regular!

158
00:09:34,230 --> 00:09:38,500
I'm terribly sorry! I'll bring you a new one!

159
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:42,490
It's okay. Don't worry about it.

160
00:09:42,490 --> 00:09:44,640
I really like ketchup anyway.

161
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:49,650
Then let's begin.

162
00:09:52,280 --> 00:09:54,660
Moe moe rock-paper-scissors!

163
00:09:54,660 --> 00:09:57,610
Rock, paper, scissors... shoot!

164
00:09:57,950 --> 00:10:03,450
MOE MOE ROCK PAPER SCISSORS 
WINNER GETS A CLEAR FILE - GET A COASTER IF YOU LOSE

165
00:09:57,950 --> 00:10:00,720
All right! I won!

166
00:10:01,290 --> 00:10:03,450
We got the clear files!

167
00:10:03,450 --> 00:10:04,890
Here you go.

168
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:08,450
Thank you!

169
00:10:08,450 --> 00:10:10,460
Oh! I got my fave!

170
00:10:10,460 --> 00:10:11,730
See? Look!

171
00:10:11,730 --> 00:10:13,070
Wow! Lucky!

172
00:10:12,280 --> 00:10:13,290
Uh-huh!

173
00:10:20,370 --> 00:10:21,640
I'm terribly sorry!

174
00:10:25,970 --> 00:10:28,410
Oh, that goes over here.

175
00:10:31,890 --> 00:10:34,080
Welcome home, Master!

176
00:10:35,460 --> 00:10:36,840
Here I go!

177
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:38,350
One, two...

178
00:10:38,350 --> 00:10:40,600
Making a pit stop...

179
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:41,810
in your...

180
00:10:41,810 --> 00:10:43,220
...heart!

181
00:10:43,870 --> 00:10:47,260
<i>Sh-She's amazing.</i>

182
00:10:47,260 --> 00:10:49,200
<i>She's really fittin' in here.</i>

183
00:10:49,580 --> 00:10:54,810
<i>I guess I'm really not 
fit for this kinda thing...</i>

184
00:10:56,230 --> 00:10:58,260
<i>Now ain't the time to feel down!</i>

185
00:10:58,680 --> 00:11:01,900
<i>I need to make sure my junior's 
first job is a success!</i>

186
00:11:03,390 --> 00:11:04,810
Um...

187
00:11:09,610 --> 00:11:11,690
Can I ask you a favor?

188
00:11:21,110 --> 00:11:23,040
Finally, break time.

189
00:11:23,500 --> 00:11:26,990
I'm glad the extra help arrived 
sooner than we expected.

190
00:11:27,400 --> 00:11:29,890
Thanks for helping out.

191
00:11:29,890 --> 00:11:32,460
No worries. I'm having fun.

192
00:11:33,250 --> 00:11:34,180
Hey.

193
00:11:34,180 --> 00:11:37,590
Do you think Senpai is pushing 
herself too far with this?

194
00:11:39,020 --> 00:11:40,840
What makes you think that?

195
00:11:40,840 --> 00:11:48,100
Clank. Clank. Clank.

196
00:11:41,290 --> 00:11:46,260
Because she moves like a robot 
every time she walks over to a table.

197
00:11:46,260 --> 00:11:47,420
True.

198
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:50,830
I'm really sorry.

199
00:11:50,830 --> 00:11:53,790
I'm causing everyone so much trouble...

200
00:11:53,790 --> 00:11:56,220
I don't think she sees it that way, though.

201
00:11:56,220 --> 00:11:57,110
Huh?

202
00:11:57,470 --> 00:12:00,030
I think she wants you to rely on her more.

203
00:12:00,030 --> 00:12:02,110
But this was my mistake, so...

204
00:12:02,590 --> 00:12:05,300
Hmm. How do I put it?

205
00:12:05,300 --> 00:12:07,950
She's even consulted with me, 
her junior, about this.

206
00:12:08,410 --> 00:12:11,950
Which proves that she cherishes you a lot.

207
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:15,850
She consulted with you?

208
00:12:16,680 --> 00:12:18,320
Yup. About this.

209
00:12:19,040 --> 00:12:21,870
But Senpai hasn't mentioned 
anything about that...

210
00:12:21,870 --> 00:12:23,350
How could she?

211
00:12:24,270 --> 00:12:27,710
Because if she did, you'd end up worrying.

212
00:12:36,980 --> 00:12:39,170
And now, the moment 
you've all been waiting for!

213
00:12:39,170 --> 00:12:42,110
It's time to begin the race!

214
00:13:26,810 --> 00:13:28,660
I'm cutting in!

215
00:13:46,810 --> 00:13:48,660
Clap your hands!

216
00:13:49,180 --> 00:13:55,210
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

217
00:13:55,210 --> 00:13:56,180
All together now!

218
00:13:57,970 --> 00:14:03,930
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

219
00:14:03,930 --> 00:14:05,360
Very good!

220
00:14:07,220 --> 00:14:09,980
Thank you!

221
00:14:10,700 --> 00:14:16,710
RACING GIRLS COLLAB CAFÉ!
OPEN TODAY

222
00:14:14,510 --> 00:14:16,710
We're open today!

223
00:14:17,080 --> 00:14:18,710
RACING GIRLS COLLAB CAFÉ
ONE FREE DRINK

224
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:20,270
You can get one free drink!

225
00:14:22,370 --> 00:14:24,460
So please take this opportunity to...

226
00:14:24,890 --> 00:14:26,350
Please come visit!

227
00:14:26,900 --> 00:14:28,280
Please come visit!

228
00:14:30,440 --> 00:14:33,600
We're the Racing Girls Collab Café!

229
00:14:34,020 --> 00:14:36,230
We're open today!

230
00:14:44,860 --> 00:14:45,940
Senpai!

231
00:14:51,170 --> 00:14:55,240
Please head back to the café 
and take a break for a bit.

232
00:14:55,700 --> 00:15:00,750
The stand-in employees are here now, 
so I can't have you do all this work...

233
00:15:01,460 --> 00:15:05,790
There's no job out there that I don't have 
to do just because I'm your senpai.

234
00:15:07,610 --> 00:15:08,660
But...

235
00:15:08,660 --> 00:15:10,380
Or, what?

236
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:14,260
Are you saying I'm not capable of 
working customer service?

237
00:15:15,290 --> 00:15:17,860
N-No! That's not what I meant.

238
00:15:19,450 --> 00:15:21,540
Please come visit!

239
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:23,020
<i>I did a lot of part-time work 
when I was younger, too!</i>

240
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:24,520
<i>This is nothing.</i>

241
00:15:24,520 --> 00:15:25,840
Please come visit!

242
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:26,730
Sorry.

243
00:15:26,730 --> 00:15:28,190
Please come visit!

244
00:15:26,730 --> 00:15:28,190
<i>It's nothing!</i>

245
00:15:30,090 --> 00:15:31,200
I'm good.

246
00:15:34,390 --> 00:15:37,120
Here you go, Master!

247
00:15:37,420 --> 00:15:40,190
Thank you!

248
00:15:41,770 --> 00:15:43,740
Please come visit!

249
00:15:44,930 --> 00:15:46,340
Amazing...

250
00:15:46,340 --> 00:15:49,520
Those girls are pros.

251
00:15:49,520 --> 00:15:50,550
Indeed.

252
00:15:51,260 --> 00:15:54,890
Why don't we leave the rest to them 
and go take a little break?

253
00:16:00,250 --> 00:16:02,060
Hey, Kamegawa.

254
00:16:02,060 --> 00:16:04,040
What is it, Senpai?

255
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:07,090
Maids are amazing.

256
00:16:05,310 --> 00:16:06,690
Please come visit!

257
00:16:06,690 --> 00:16:07,770
Here you go.

258
00:16:07,090 --> 00:16:08,230
They are.

259
00:16:09,010 --> 00:16:11,700
I just can't get into character.

260
00:16:11,700 --> 00:16:13,910
Yeah, they're really impressive.

261
00:16:14,340 --> 00:16:17,630
It's also amazing how she's able 
to perform so well no matter what.

262
00:16:18,190 --> 00:16:19,780
Do you mean Hotta?

263
00:16:19,780 --> 00:16:22,690
Yeah, she did surprisingly well.

264
00:16:22,690 --> 00:16:24,460
She's ignoring the whole concept, though.

265
00:16:25,150 --> 00:16:27,690
I, on the other hand, haven't done anything.

266
00:16:27,690 --> 00:16:29,300
No! That's not true!

267
00:16:30,900 --> 00:16:35,260
This café was able to open thanks to you.

268
00:16:36,250 --> 00:16:39,010
And the customers genuinely 
seem to be enjoying themselves!

269
00:16:42,460 --> 00:16:48,020
I'm so happy that the first job assigned 
to me turned out the way it did.

270
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:55,530
And because you're here, Hotta and 
I are motivated to work even harder!

271
00:16:56,220 --> 00:17:01,290
Isn't that just because me 
being here puts pressure on you?

272
00:17:01,610 --> 00:17:03,080
What? Um...

273
00:17:05,460 --> 00:17:07,540
HMM...

274
00:17:10,970 --> 00:17:13,050
I can't swim!

275
00:17:13,550 --> 00:17:14,300
Say what?

276
00:17:14,670 --> 00:17:17,320
I-I can only manage 15 meters at best.

277
00:17:17,320 --> 00:17:20,100
When I try to kick my feet, I just sink.

278
00:17:20,100 --> 00:17:22,720
And I still can't eat peppers.

279
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:26,800
I always procrastinated on my summer 
homework until the last day of summer.

280
00:17:26,800 --> 00:17:29,190
I've never won a fight with my siblings.

281
00:17:29,190 --> 00:17:30,760
My hair is super curly.

282
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:33,480
I frantically straighten it 
with an iron every morning!

283
00:17:34,430 --> 00:17:35,670
An iron...

284
00:17:37,270 --> 00:17:38,300
Wait.

285
00:17:38,300 --> 00:17:41,730
When you sometimes show up 
with a wavy hair style...

286
00:17:41,730 --> 00:17:43,140
That's not on purpose?

287
00:17:43,140 --> 00:17:45,640
There's no saving it on humid days.

288
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:46,580
Oh, also...

289
00:17:47,950 --> 00:17:51,540
You have quite the human
 side to you after all.

290
00:17:52,600 --> 00:17:55,380
Thanks for saying all that for my sake.

291
00:17:57,620 --> 00:18:01,150
Even so, we can't just keep 
resting here the whole time.

292
00:18:02,490 --> 00:18:06,820
I need to perfect being a maid to make up 
for how much trouble we caused.

293
00:18:07,740 --> 00:18:11,750
Not that there's gonna be any 
demand for me as a maid.

294
00:18:14,260 --> 00:18:15,450
There is!

295
00:18:15,450 --> 00:18:16,280
Huh?

296
00:18:16,280 --> 00:18:18,400
<i>Why did I just blurt that out?</i>

297
00:18:18,820 --> 00:18:22,200
Y-You don't need to worry 
about me that much.

298
00:18:22,200 --> 00:18:23,870
That's not what I...

299
00:18:23,870 --> 00:18:25,540
Let's get going.

300
00:18:47,520 --> 00:18:48,250
Like this?

301
00:18:49,020 --> 00:18:51,470
That's not it.

302
00:18:50,590 --> 00:18:51,470
This?

303
00:18:52,580 --> 00:18:54,080
How's this?

304
00:18:54,080 --> 00:18:55,850
Um... Sorry, but...

305
00:18:55,850 --> 00:18:57,420
It's more like this!

306
00:18:57,420 --> 00:18:58,540
Um...

307
00:18:59,210 --> 00:19:00,190
This?

308
00:19:00,990 --> 00:19:03,300
No, like this!

309
00:19:01,300 --> 00:19:03,500
What's she doing?

310
00:19:03,500 --> 00:19:04,540
Is she in a bind?

311
00:19:04,540 --> 00:19:05,780
This is hard...

312
00:19:05,780 --> 00:19:06,460
This!

313
00:19:06,460 --> 00:19:07,050
This?

314
00:19:07,050 --> 00:19:07,800
No!

315
00:19:07,800 --> 00:19:08,950
Like this!

316
00:19:15,380 --> 00:19:18,850
What are you doing to our maid?

317
00:19:18,850 --> 00:19:20,000
Senpai!

318
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,120
Wrong approach!

319
00:19:21,120 --> 00:19:22,760
You're taking the wrong approach!

320
00:19:27,140 --> 00:19:29,060
Thank you!

321
00:19:29,060 --> 00:19:31,140
That's it! That!

322
00:19:31,610 --> 00:19:33,650
Er... Uh-huh...

323
00:19:33,650 --> 00:19:37,790
Wow, I'm so glad I came today! Really!

324
00:19:37,790 --> 00:19:41,110
Oh. I'd like to order a parfait, too.

325
00:19:41,440 --> 00:19:43,110
Oh... Of course.

326
00:19:43,110 --> 00:19:45,870
And also a Moe Moe Rock-Paper-Scissors.

327
00:19:45,870 --> 00:19:48,060
With the same angry energy you just had.

328
00:19:48,060 --> 00:19:50,760
Th-Thank you for your patronage.

329
00:19:52,840 --> 00:19:56,630
Thanks so much for your work today!

330
00:19:56,630 --> 00:20:00,070
The extra girls made it, 
so we should be good now.

331
00:20:01,630 --> 00:20:04,520
Again, we're sorry for all the trouble.

332
00:20:04,520 --> 00:20:05,790
Not at all.

333
00:20:05,790 --> 00:20:08,640
Your maid service was amazing, as well!

334
00:20:09,540 --> 00:20:11,500
Thank you very much.

335
00:20:16,410 --> 00:20:20,620
I'm glad the first day went smoothly somehow.

336
00:20:17,650 --> 00:20:21,150
TOUCHING IS NOT ALLOWED!

337
00:20:22,610 --> 00:20:24,570
It's thanks to you, Senpai!

338
00:20:27,300 --> 00:20:29,160
Well, let's head home.

339
00:20:29,160 --> 00:20:30,100
Yes, ma'am!

340
00:20:32,170 --> 00:20:34,920
Hey, about that customer earlier...

341
00:20:34,920 --> 00:20:37,340
Why did he seem so happy about me?

342
00:20:37,340 --> 00:20:38,620
Well, because...

343
00:20:42,050 --> 00:20:47,050
TOUCHING IS NOT ALLOWED!

344
00:20:47,050 --> 00:20:48,590
So that's why!

345
00:20:53,250 --> 00:20:54,340
Do I look like her?

346
00:20:55,270 --> 00:20:58,380
I guess you do have a slight resemblance.

347
00:20:58,750 --> 00:20:59,520
But...

348
00:20:59,520 --> 00:21:01,100
But what?

349
00:21:01,100 --> 00:21:02,980
Er, well...

350
00:21:02,980 --> 00:21:08,910
You seem more like a master 
than a maid, I guess.

351
00:21:09,320 --> 00:21:11,040
What's that supposed to mean?

352
00:21:11,670 --> 00:21:14,050
To me, you're my senior,

353
00:21:14,050 --> 00:21:16,760
someone who looks after me in various ways.

354
00:21:17,720 --> 00:21:22,550
So I can't imagine you as someone
who would call another person "Master."

355
00:21:23,510 --> 00:21:26,550
Aren't maids the ones who look after others?

356
00:21:26,550 --> 00:21:27,280
Huh?

357
00:21:27,980 --> 00:21:29,800
I guess you're right.

358
00:21:33,020 --> 00:21:34,190
There you are!

359
00:21:34,190 --> 00:21:36,770
What are you two doing here?

360
00:21:36,770 --> 00:21:38,220
Oh, sorry.

361
00:21:38,220 --> 00:21:40,340
We're just having a little pity party.

362
00:21:40,340 --> 00:21:41,770
Pity party?

363
00:21:41,770 --> 00:21:43,700
What are you saying?

364
00:21:43,700 --> 00:21:45,370
Today was a great success!

365
00:21:45,370 --> 00:21:48,570
We're going to let loose 
and go drinking after this!

366
00:21:48,570 --> 00:21:52,580
Hurry and get dressed 
before the stores get too busy!

367
00:21:54,360 --> 00:21:57,330
It's time to go, Master!

368
00:22:00,700 --> 00:22:04,210
I-If you're not going, I'm leaving you!

369
00:22:04,210 --> 00:22:05,720
Ah, wait!

370
00:22:05,720 --> 00:22:07,590
Please wait for me!

371
00:22:06,010 --> 00:22:10,970
IF YOU WON'T FOLLOW ME, I'M LEAVING YOU!

